1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,700
Feed is the largest cost on a shrimp farm — and
the easiest thing to get wrong.

2
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,600
Too little, and growth stalls.

3
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:20,000
Too much, and you pay for feed that sinks and
never becomes shrimp.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,300
Most small farms still feed by habit: a fixed
timer, a fixed scoop, a fixed time of day.

5
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:37,200
But a pond is not fixed. Biomass changes.
Appetite changes. Water changes.

6
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:43,000
And when the signal drops, the schedule keeps
running anyway.

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,200
Samples live in notebooks.

8
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:55,000
By harvest, nobody can say what was fed, what it
produced, or what to change next cycle.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,500
PakaonAI starts from a different premise: the
pond should decide the ration.

10
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:12,500
A controller at the pond. A dashboard in your
hand. A record that survives the season.

11
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:22,600
At the edge, an ESP32 runs the feeder: auger,
relay, real-time clock, hopper sensor,
temperature probe.

12
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:30,700
It keeps its own schedule, so feeding does not
depend on the network.

13
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:42,000
In the cloud, samples become biomass, biomass
becomes a ration, and rations become a schedule
you can adjust.

14
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,600
The loop starts with a sample. Weigh a few
shrimp, count the pond, and log it.

15
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:58,100
PakaonAI computes average weight, estimated
biomass, and the feed your pond should receive
today.

16
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:04,000
Set meals per day, a feeding window, and a daily
cap.

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,900
The schedule previews the dose before you save
it.

18
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:18,000
When the feeder runs, every dose is recorded
with its trigger: scheduled, remote, or the
physical button.

19
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
At harvest, those records become feed conversion
ratio. Not a guess. A calculation.

20
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:34,900
Connectivity in the field is not a guarantee, so
PakaonAI installs as an app and keeps working
offline.

21
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:39,200
Dashboard snapshots, schedule, growth, and
history stay readable.

22
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:45,800
Biomass samples queue locally and replay when
the connection returns, without double-counting.

23
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:49,100
What does not queue is deliberate.

24
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:55,100
Feed commands, schedule edits, harvest, and
calibration require a live connection.

25
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:59,000
Feeding itself continues on the controller's
clock.

26
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:05,000
And Pakoy reads the pond context you are allowed
to see.

27
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,900
PakaonAI is multi-tenant by design. The
organization is the tenant boundary.

28
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:15,200
Below it: membership, farms, ponds, and devices,
each scoped on the server.

29
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:19,200
A pond owns its cycles, samples, schedules, and
devices.

30
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:26,700
Roles are scoped: owner, admin, operator,
viewer. A viewer can read the pond but not
change it.

31
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:29,400
Platform administrators sit above every tenant.

32
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:35,200
The actions that matter require a reason, are
written to an audit log,

33
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:38,300
and destructive actions require a fresh
password.

34
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,000
Devices are provisioned deliberately.

35
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,500
An administrator registers the unit to an
organization and pond.

36
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:52,000
Then the controller raises its own setup
network, and you scan for Wi-Fi and save the
identity.

37
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:01,600
We assessed the system against the eight
characteristics of ISO/IEC 25010, as an
engineering self-assessment, not a
certification.

38
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:04,800
Three thousand three hundred automated tests.

39
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:09,000
Ninety-two percent line coverage on the
application library.

40
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:16,500
End-to-end runs, cross-browser smoke tests,
accessibility checks with zero violations on the
audited surfaces.

41
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:25,000
And a restore drill that passes in CI. Where a
gap remains, it is written down.

42
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,900
The market problem is real: feed dominates
operating cost,

43
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:36,900
and most small farms have no defensible record
of how it was used.

44
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:45,000
PakaonAI does not promise a yield. It makes the
feeding decision visible, repeatable, and
reviewable.

45
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,300
This is a research prototype. Accounts are
issued by the team.

46
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:56,000
Growth and feed-conversion results are still
under review.

47
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,000
PakaonAI. Built at ISUFST. Feed on evidence.
